    "number": "Ch 12",
    "title": "Important Laws (frequently asked in exams)",
    "grade": "11",
    "subject": "maths",
    "description": "**Commutative Law**",
    "topics": [
      "Core concept",
      "Application",
      "Formulas"
    ],
    "analogy": "```\nA ∪ B = B ∪ A\nA ∩ B = B ∩ A\n```\n**Associative Law**\n```\n(A ∪ B) ∪ C = A ∪ (B ∪ C)\n(A ∩ B) ∩ C = A ∩ (B ∩ C)\n```\n**De Morgan's Laws** (very important, frequently tested)\n```\n(A ∪ B)′ = A′ ∩ B′\n(A ∩ B)′ = A′ ∪ B′\n```\n**Distributive Law**\n```\nA ∪ (B ∩ C) = (A ∪ B) ∩ (A ∪ C)\nA ∩ (B ∪ C) = (A ∩ B) ∪ (A ∩ C)\n```\n---",
    "syntax": "N/A",
    "codeExample": "No example provided.",
    "pitfalls": "None reported.",
